spec ww11-ring-8: 8 sessions, 2 permutations
# WW11. A ring of 8 transactions, each writing its own node and then its
# successor's — the N-way deadlock cycle. No step may ever wait (F7); each write
# succeeds or is refused. Every transaction then rolls back and the vacuum is drained
# (H1), after which one autocommit statement rewrites the whole ring and must
# succeed: the cycle leaves nothing behind that blocks progress. Named interleavings:
# round-robin, sequential.

starting permutation: s0b s1b s2b s3b s4b s5b s6b s7b s0own s1own s2own s3own s4own s5own s6own s7own s0next s1next s2next s3next s4next s5next s6next s7next s0rb s0dr s1rb s1dr s2rb s2dr s3rb s3dr s4rb s4dr s5rb s5dr s6rb s6dr s7rb s7dr retry
step s0b: BEGIN
step s1b: BEGIN
step s2b: BEGIN
step s3b: BEGIN
step s4b: BEGIN
step s5b: BEGIN
step s6b: BEGIN
step s7b: BEGIN
step s0own: MATCH (n:Ring {name:'r0'}) SET n.v = 's0' RETURN n.v AS v
v   
